# Phase L3 (docs/nvidia-native.md): NVIDIA's own Vulkan driver as the device's Vulkan driver, on
# the entry with androidboot.hardware.vulkan=nvidia (the "NVIDIA (proprietary)" entry,
# androidboot.android_pc.gpu=nvidia).
#
# - ro.hardware.vulkan=nvidia comes from the bootconfig (init_graphics.vendor.rc). The loader must
#   open /vendor/lib64/hw/vulkan.nvidia.so in the sphal linker namespace, where nvglibc and
#   NVIDIA's libraries (/vendor/lib64/nvidia) are visible, not from the Cuttlefish Vulkan APEX:
#   ro.vulkan.apex is set empty here, before that APEX's `on init` sets it.
# - HWUI draws with Skia on Vulkan (androidboot.hardware.guest_hwui_renderer=skiavk), and so does
#   SurfaceFlinger's RenderEngine (below). GLES (boot animation, GL apps) is ANGLE on the same
#   Vulkan driver.
# - minigbm's "nvidia" backend gives every buffer the layout vulkan.nvidia expects when
#   ro.hardware.vulkan is nvidia.
# There is no CPU fallback: when NVIDIA's driver fails, SurfaceFlinger fails, and logcat says why
# (tags vulkan.nvidia, nvglibc, SurfaceFlinger, RenderEngine).
on early-init && property:ro.boot.hardware.vulkan=nvidia
    setprop ro.vulkan.apex ""
    setprop debug.renderengine.backend skiavkthreaded
